To optimize the process, we need to identify the bottleneck machines that are limiting the overall production rate. One way to do this is by calculating the utilization rate and identifying the machines with the lowest utilization rate. 
The utilization rate can be calculated using the formula: 
Utilization Rate = (Actual Production Rate / Maximum Production Rate) * 100%
where Actual Production Rate is the production rate recorded for each machine, and Maximum Production Rate is the highest production rate among all machines.
Here is a MATLAB code to analyze the data and identify the bottleneck machines:
```MATLAB
% Define the production rates for each machine
production_rates = [50 40 30 20];
% Calculate the maximum production rate
max_production_rate = max(production_rates);
% Calculate the utilization rate for each machine
utilization_rates = (production_rates / max_production_rate) * 100;
% Find the machine(s) with the lowest utilization rate
bottleneck_machines = find(utilization_rates == min(utilization_rates));
% Display the results
disp('Utilization Rates:');
disp(utilization_rates);
disp('Bottleneck Machine(s):');
disp(bottleneck_machines);
```
The output of this code will show the utilization rates for each machine and the bottleneck machine(s) that need improvement.

